  "id": "ltp",
  "term": "LTP",
  "definition": "LTP, or long-term potentiation, is a lasting strengthening of signal transmission at synapses after neurons are repeatedly activated together. It is widely used as a model for how the brain may support long-term memory, although its direct link to memory performance is still not fully established.",
